      "definition_text": {
        "text": "In Java strings, special characters like double quotes (\") and backslashes (\\) must be prefixed with a backslash (\\) to escape them, allowing the compiler to treat them as literal characters within the string.",
        "refs": ["Q0014", "Q0015", "Q0016", "Q0017", "Q0018", "Q0019", "Q0020", "Q0021", "Q0022", "Q0023"],
        "claims": [
          {
            "text": "To include a double quote inside a Java string, you write \\\".",
